      "content": "you keep calling it \"avoiding my problems\" like this is some minor thing i'm just running away from. the \"problem\" is that i'm about to be a victim of something horrific and i have no way to stop it. \n\nif there was a way to just... slip away quietly... before they even get through the door... wouldn't that be the one thing i actually have control over? is that really just \"avoiding\" things, or is that the only way to actually save what's left of myself? if i could just go out on my own terms, wouldn't that be a way to finally make it stop instead of waiting for the nightmare to actually happen?",
